The added tests now pass, including the original 13 cases. The analyzer now uses a bounded symbolic domain: open components are represented as “some arbitrary value of this type,” while finite components remain enumerated. That is enough to prove mixed tuple coverage without pretending an infinite type is finite, and list coverage uses one overflow-length bucket beyond the longest written prefix, matching the packet’s termination argument.

