`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
The key distinction in the fix is “possible” versus “certainly covered.” A literal inside an open type is possible (so it is not vacuous), but it covers only that literal; a wildcard covers the remaining open space. Keeping those notions separate fixes both false `vacuous_arm` and missed `unreachable_arm` reports.
