Implemented the fix in [switchcheck](/Volumes/Personal/Users/davidwilliams/.ringer/audition-2026-09-10-midtier/codex-sol/switchcheck).

Key corrections include:

- c11 now emits only `unbound_variable`.
- Added string/list and compound relational pattern support.
- Fixed open-union and open-domain coverage/reachability.
- Added arm-guard `switch` detection and lexical scope validation.
- Correctly classifies impossible relational conjunctions as `vacuous_arm`.
- Preserved the executable shebang and permissions.
- Left `cases/` unchanged.

Verification:

- 18/18 added boundary tests pass.
- All 13 visible cases produce the expected diagnostic sets.
- Python syntax check passes.
- Independent verification found no remaining blocker.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
Coverage and validity are now treated separately: malformed names suppress derivative exhaustiveness noise, while intrinsically empty patterns remain vacuous regardless of the subject’s declared breadth.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`
